# Multiplayer Development Guidelines for TrapDash

This guide outlines the specific considerations and patterns for implementing multiplayer functionality in the TrapDash game.

## Core Multiplayer Architecture

*   **Firebase Integration**: All multiplayer functionality uses Firebase services via CDN integration in `[index.html](mdc:index.html)`.
    *   **Realtime Database**: Game state synchronization, room management, player data
    *   **Authentication**: Anonymous authentication for immediate play (mobile-friendly)
    *   **Cloud Functions**: Server-side validation and anti-cheat measures

*   **Network Synchronization**: Handled by `[js/NetworkSynchronizer.js](mdc:js/NetworkSynchronizer.js)`
    *   Position broadcasting optimized for mobile networks
    *   Event synchronization (power-ups, collisions, finish line)
    *   Adaptive sync rates based on network conditions
    *   Client-side prediction with server reconciliation

## Mobile-First Design Principles

*   **Touch Interface Optimization**: All multiplayer UI must use minimum 44pt touch targets
*   **Network Efficiency**: Optimize all communications for mobile data usage and varying network quality
*   **Responsive Design**: Support various mobile screen sizes and orientations
*   **Connection Management**: Handle airplane mode, background app scenarios, and network switching

## Game State Management

*   **Deterministic Behavior**: All bot AI and game mechanics must be deterministic across clients
*   **Shared State Object**: Centralized game state that can be synchronized across all players
*   **Mode Detection**: Automatic detection between single-player and multiplayer modes
*   **Graceful Degradation**: Fallback to single-player when multiplayer services unavailable

## Room and Lobby System

*   **Room Management**: Handled by `[js/LobbyScene.js](mdc:js/LobbyScene.js)`
    *   4-6 digit room codes for easy mobile sharing
    *   Quick Match and Create Room options
    *   Player ready/not ready status tracking
    *   Auto-cleanup after 5 minutes of inactivity

*   **Matchmaking**: Queue-based system for Quick Match
    *   Bot filling when fewer than 4 players
    *   Timeout mechanisms for abandoned rooms
    *   Host migration capabilities

## Security and Anti-Cheat

*   **Server-Side Validation**: All critical game events validated via Cloud Functions
    *   Movement bounds and speed limits
    *   Power-up usage timing and cooldowns
    *   Finish line crossing legitimacy
    *   Basic anti-speed-hack protection

*   **Rate Limiting**: Prevent spam and abuse of Firebase operations
*   **Fraud Detection**: Monitor for suspicious player behavior patterns

## Performance Optimization

*   **Asset Management**: Shared asset loading for multiplayer sessions
*   **Connection Pooling**: Efficient Firebase connection management
*   **Delta Compression**: Minimize network traffic for mobile devices
*   **Adaptive Quality**: Adjust game quality based on device performance and network conditions

## Error Handling and Recovery

*   **Reconnection Logic**: Robust handling of mobile network switching
*   **Game State Backup**: Local backup for disconnection recovery
*   **Partial Disconnections**: Handle scenarios where some players lose connection
*   **Diagnostic Tools**: Network troubleshooting and monitoring capabilities

## Testing Requirements

*   **Multi-Device Testing**: Test across various mobile devices and network conditions
*   **Stress Testing**: Validate 4-player scenarios under load
*   **Edge Case Testing**: Room management, host disconnection, network failures
*   **Latency Testing**: Synchronization accuracy across different latency conditions

## Implementation Phases

Refer to `[IMPLEMENTATION_TRACKER.md](mdc:IMPLEMENTATION_TRACKER.md)` phases 12-19 for detailed multiplayer implementation roadmap:
